   READING: on the committed driver the last program record is at cycle 1052 in ALL THREE runs, including the
   one given sixteen times the wait. The extra time bought 38888 more debug-ROM records and ZERO program
   progress, which is what makes this a livelock rather than a slow run or a tight bound.

== 3. THE DRIVER'S OWN COUNTERS: the leak is visible even on a seed that PASSED ==
   Requests against releases, from each run's own report line. The failing runs print none, because the
   cocotb assertion aborts the test before the UVM report phase, which is itself worth knowing.
   BEFORE, on the probe run at seed 1 that PASSED:
     GEN_DBG] requests=39 releases=38
     one request never released: it passed only because the program reached its store first.
   AFTER, on the fixed driver:
     seed 700483392: GEN_DBG] requests=54 releases=54
     seed 1:         GEN_DBG] requests=46 releases=46
     every request released, in both. The counts differ between runs because they are different builds and
     different seeds; the invariant to read is requests EQUALS releases, not the absolute figures.

